# Product documentation alignment

When you **add** or **materially change** user-facing or cross-cutting behavior (routes, permissions, data flows, booking lifecycle, admin flows), update project docs in the **same task** unless the user explicitly limits scope to code only.

**Methodology:** [`docs/meta/ai_first_project_methodology.md`](docs/meta/ai_first_project_methodology.md) — §3.4 product-docs-alignment, §2.2 agent cycle VERIFICATION step.

## What to do

1. **Compare** implemented behavior with PRD, user flows, and design artifacts.
2. **Update the smallest set** of files that describe that surface.
3. If behavior intentionally diverges — update docs to match new truth.

## Where to look and update

| Topic | Files |
|-------|--------|
| Scope / MVP | [`docs/default_docs/fitness-platform-mvp.md`](docs/default_docs/fitness-platform-mvp.md), future `mvp_scope.md` |
| User journeys | [`docs/prds/01_product_scope/user_flows/users_mvp/`](docs/prds/01_product_scope/user_flows/users_mvp/) |
| Routes / IA | [`docs/design/canonical_routes.md`](docs/design/canonical_routes.md) |
| Contracts | [`docs/implementation/mvp/contracts/`](docs/implementation/mvp/contracts/) |
| Database | [`docs/prds/03_data_model/database_schema_v1.md`](docs/prds/03_data_model/database_schema_v1.md) |
| Authorization | [`docs/prds/04_authorization_privacy/`](docs/prds/04_authorization_privacy/) (when created) |
| Governance | ADRs in [`docs/prds/07_governance/`](docs/prds/07_governance/) |

## Precedence

Follow source-of-truth order in [`pulse-project-context.mdc`](pulse-project-context.mdc).

## Scope boundary

Pure refactors with no observable behavior change — doc updates optional unless fixing factual errors.
